-- src:13222 | (2) An accused who is convicted under this section is not liable to be tried again for the offence that he was charged with attempting to commit.
@ref s 661(2) (src:13222-13222)
GIVEN `the accused is convicted under section 661` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 661(2) the accused is liable to be tried again for the offence the accused was charged with attempting to commit` MEANS
    IF `the accused is convicted under section 661`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An accused who is convicted under this section is not liable to be tried again for the offence that he was charged with attempting to commit" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is convicted under this section"

§ `Section 662 -- Offence charged, part only proved`

-- src:13224 | 662 (1) A count in an indictment is divisible and where the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, the accused may be convicted
@ref s 662(1) (src:13224-13224)
GIVEN `the count is a count in an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(1) a count in an indictment is divisible` MEANS
    IF `the count is a count in an indictment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A count in an indictment is divisible"

-- src:13224 | 662 (1) A count in an indictment is divisible and where the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, the accused may be convicted
-- src:13225 | (a) of an offence so included that is proved, notwithstanding that the whole offence that is charged is not proved; or
@ref s 662(1)(a) (src:13224-13225)
GIVEN `the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the included offence is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(1)(a) the accused may be convicted of the included offence that is proved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, the accused may be convicted" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the included offence is proved` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of an offence so included that is proved, notwithstanding that the whole offence that is charged is not proved"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13224 | 662 (1) A count in an indictment is divisible and where the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, the accused may be convicted
-- src:13225 | (a) of an offence so included that is proved, notwithstanding that the whole offence that is charged is not proved; or
-- src:13226 | (b) of an attempt to commit an offence so included.
@ref s 662(1)(b) (src:13224-13226)
GIVEN `the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes an attempt to commit the included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(1)(b) the accused may be convicted of an attempt to commit the included offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the commission of the offence charged, as described in the enactment creating it or as charged in the count, includes the commission of another offence, whether punishable by indictment or on summary conviction, the accused may be convicted" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the evidence establishes an attempt to commit the included offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of an attempt to commit an offence so included"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) to (7): "for greater certainty" clauses repeat what subsection (1) already allows; a case outside their own facts is not decided by them, so they answer NOTHING there, not JUST FALSE (fork line [F:greater-certainty]). Subsections (3), (4) and (6) carry no such words.
-- src:13228 | (2) For greater certainty and without limiting the generality of subsection (1), where a count charges first degree murder and the evidence does not prove first degree murder but proves second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder, the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder, as the case may be.
@ref s 662(2) (src:13228-13228)
DECLARE `s 662(2) what the evidence proves` IS ONE OF
    `s 662(2) first degree murder`
    `s 662(2) second degree murder`
    `s 662(2) an attempt to commit second degree murder`
    `s 662(2) none of these`

-- src:13228 | (2) For greater certainty and without limiting the generality of subsection (1), where a count charges first degree murder and the evidence does not prove first degree murder but proves second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder, the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder, as the case may be.
@ref s 662(2) (src:13228-13228)
GIVEN `the offence the count charges` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `what the evidence proves` IS A `s 662(2) what the evidence proves`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(2) the jury may find the accused not guilty of first degree murder but guilty of second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder` MEANS
    IF `the offence the count charges` EQUALS `first degree murder` AND (`what the evidence proves` EQUALS `s 662(2) second degree murder` OR `what the evidence proves` EQUALS `s 662(2) an attempt to commit second degree murder`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For greater certainty and without limiting the generality of subsection (1), where a count charges first degree murder and the evidence does not prove first degree murder but proves second degree murder or an attempt to commit second degree murder" [F:greater-certainty]

-- src:13230 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), where a count charges murder and the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide but does not prove murder, the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide, but shall not on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence.
@ref s 662(3) (src:13230-13230)
GIVEN `the count charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves murder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(3) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide` MEANS
    IF `the count charges murder` AND `the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide` AND (NOT `the evidence proves murder`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a count charges murder and the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide but does not prove murder, the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:13230 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), where a count charges murder and the evidence proves manslaughter or infanticide but does not prove murder, the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder but guilty of manslaughter or infanticide, but shall not on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence.
@ref s 662(3) (src:13230-13230)
GIVEN `the count charges murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(3) the jury may on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the count charges murder` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a count charges murder"
        IF `subsection (4) applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (4)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not on that count find the accused guilty of any other offence" [M-a]

-- src:13232 | (4) Where a count charges the murder of a child or infanticide and the evidence proves the commission of an offence under section 243 but does not prove murder or infanticide, the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide, as the case may be, but guilty of an offence under section 243.
@ref s 662(4) (src:13232-13232)
GIVEN `the count charges the murder of a child or infanticide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves the commission of an offence under section 243` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves murder or infanticide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(4) the jury may find the accused not guilty of murder or infanticide but guilty of an offence under section 243` MEANS
    IF `the count charges the murder of a child or infanticide` AND `the evidence proves the commission of an offence under section 243` AND (NOT `the evidence proves murder or infanticide`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a count charges the murder of a child or infanticide and the evidence proves the commission of an offence under section 243 but does not prove murder or infanticide, the jury may find the accused not guilty" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:13234 | (5) For greater certainty, when a count charges an offence under section 220, 221 or 236 arising out of the operation of a conveyance, and the evidence does not prove that offence but proves an offence under section 320.13, the accused may be convicted of an offence under that section.
@ref s 662(5) (src:13234-13234)
GIVEN `the count charges an offence under section 220, 221 or 236 arising out of the operation of a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves an offence under section 320.13` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(5) the accused may be convicted of an offence under section 320.13` MEANS
    IF `the count charges an offence under section 220, 221 or 236 arising out of the operation of a conveyance` AND (NOT `the evidence proves that offence`) AND `the evidence proves an offence under section 320.13`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For greater certainty, when a count charges an offence under section 220, 221 or 236 arising out of the operation of a conveyance, and the evidence does not prove that offence but proves an offence under section 320.13" [F:greater-certainty]

-- src:13236 | (5.1) For greater certainty, if a count charges an offence under subsection 263.1(1) and the evidence does not prove that offence but proves an included offence, the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved.
@ref s 662(5.1) (src:13236-13236)
GIVEN `the count charges an offence under subsection 263.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence proves an included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 662(5.1) the accused may be found guilty of the offence that is proved` MEANS
    IF `the count charges an offence under subsection 263.1(1)` AND (NOT `the evidence proves that offence`) AND `the evidence proves an included offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For greater certainty, if a count charges an offence under subsection 263.1(1) and the evidence does not prove that offence but proves an included offence" [F:greater-certainty]

