§ `Section 663 -- Infanticide: no acquittal unless act or omission not wilful`

-- src:13242 | 663 Where a female person is charged with infanticide and the evidence establishes that she caused the death of her child but does not establish that, at the time of the act or omission by which she caused the death of the child,
-- src:13243 | (a) she was not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child or from the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child, and
-- src:13244 | (b) the balance of her mind was, at that time, disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the child or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child,
-- src:13245 | she may be convicted unless the evidence establishes that the act or omission was not wilful.
@ref s 663 (src:13242-13245)
GIVEN `a female person is charged with infanticide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes that she caused the death of her child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes that, at the time of the act or omission, she was not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child or from the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes that, at that time, the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the child or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence establishes that the act or omission was not wilful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 663 the female person may be convicted of infanticide` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a female person is charged with infanticide` AND `the evidence establishes that she caused the death of her child`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a female person is charged with infanticide and the evidence establishes that she caused the death of her child" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF `the evidence establishes that, at the time of the act or omission, she was not fully recovered from the effects of giving birth to the child or from the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child` AND `the evidence establishes that, at that time, the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the child or of the effect of lactation consequent on the birth of the child` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not establish that, at the time of the act or omission by which she caused the death of the child, (a) she was not fully recovered ... and (b) the balance of her mind was, at that time, disturbed" (both are established) [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF `the evidence establishes that the act or omission was not wilful` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she may be convicted unless the evidence establishes that the act or omission was not wilful" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 664 to 669 -- Previous convictions`

-- src:13249 | 664 No indictment in respect of an offence for which, by reason of previous convictions, a greater punishment may be imposed shall contain any reference to previous convictions.
@ref s 664 (src:13249-13249)
GIVEN `the indictment is in respect of an offence for which, by reason of previous convictions, a greater punishment may be imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 664 the section bars the indictment from containing any reference to previous convictions` MEANS
    IF `the indictment is in respect of an offence for which, by reason of previous convictions, a greater punishment may be imposed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No indictment in respect of an offence for which, by reason of previous convictions, a greater punishment may be imposed shall contain any reference to previous convictions"

-- src:13250 | 665 [Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 3]
@ref s 665 (repealed) (src:13250-13250)
`s 665 what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 3]"

-- src:13252 | 666 Where, at a trial, the accused adduces evidence of his good character, the prosecutor may, in answer thereto, before a verdict is returned, adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused for any offences, including any previous conviction by reason of which a greater punishment may be imposed.
@ref s 666 (src:13252-13252)
GIVEN `the accused adduces evidence of the accused’s good character at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor adduces the evidence in answer to the evidence of good character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a verdict has been returned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 666 the prosecutor may adduce evidence of the previous conviction of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused adduces evidence of the accused’s good character at the trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, at a trial, the accused adduces evidence of his good character, the prosecutor may" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF `a verdict has been returned` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before a verdict is returned" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the prosecutor adduces the evidence in answer to the evidence of good character` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in answer thereto"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 667 -- Proof of previous conviction`

DECLARE `s 667(1)(a) the signer of the certificate` IS ONE OF
    `s 667(1)(a)(i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt`
    `s 667(1)(a)(ii) the clerk of the court in which the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt was made`
    `s 667(1)(a)(iii) a fingerprint examiner`
    `s 667(1)(a) some other signer`

-- src:13254 | 667 (1) In any proceedings,
-- src:13255 | (a) a certificate setting out with reasonable particularity the conviction or discharge under section 730, the finding of guilt under the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, the finding of guilt under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the conviction and sentence or finding of guilt and sentence in Canada of an offender is, on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate, evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced, without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate, if it is signed by
-- src:13256 | (i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt,
-- src:13257 | (ii) the clerk of the court in which the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt was made, or
-- src:13258 | (iii) a fingerprint examiner;
@ref s 667(1)(a) (src:13254-13258)
GIVEN `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity the conviction or discharge under section 730, the finding of guilt under the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, the finding of guilt under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the conviction and sentence or finding of guilt and sentence in Canada of an offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      signer IS A `s 667(1)(a) the signer of the certificate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(1)(a) the certificate is evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted, so discharged or so convicted and sentenced or found guilty and sentenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the certificate sets out with reasonable particularity the conviction or discharge under section 730, the finding of guilt under the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, the finding of guilt under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the conviction and sentence or finding of guilt and sentence in Canada of an offender` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate setting out with reasonable particularity the conviction or discharge under section 730, the finding of guilt under the Young Offenders Act, chapter Y-1 of the Revised Statutes of Canada, 1985, the finding of guilt under the Youth Criminal Justice Act or the conviction and sentence or finding of guilt and sentence in Canada of an offender"
        IF NOT `it is proved that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate, evidence that the accused or defendant was so convicted" [M-a]
        IF signer EQUALS `s 667(1)(a) some other signer` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is signed by (i) the person who made the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt, (ii) the clerk of the court in which the conviction, order for the discharge or finding of guilt was made, or (iii) a fingerprint examiner" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13259 | (b) evidence that the fingerprints of the accused or defendant are the same as the fingerprints of the offender whose fingerprints are reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii) is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate;
@ref s 667(1)(b) (src:13259-13259)
GIVEN `there is evidence that the fingerprints of the accused or defendant are the same as the fingerprints of the offender whose fingerprints are reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(1)(b) the fingerprint evidence is proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is evidence that the fingerprints of the accused or defendant are the same as the fingerprints of the offender whose fingerprints are reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "evidence that the fingerprints of the accused or defendant are the same as the fingerprints of the offender whose fingerprints are reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii)"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in that certificate" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13260 | (c) a certificate of a fingerprint examiner stating that he has compared the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to that certificate with the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii) and that they are those of the same person is evidence of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate; and
@ref s 667(1)(c) (src:13260-13260)
GIVEN `the certificate is a certificate of a fingerprint examiner stating that he has compared the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to that certificate with the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii) and that they are those of the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(1)(c) the certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed it` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is a certificate of a fingerprint examiner stating that he has compared the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to that certificate with the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii) and that they are those of the same person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate of a fingerprint examiner stating that he has compared the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to that certificate with the fingerprints reproduced in or attached to a certificate issued under subparagraph (a)(iii) and that they are those of the same person"

-- src:13261 | (d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii) may be in Form 44, and a certificate under paragraph (c) may be in Form 45.
@ref s 667(1)(d) (src:13261-13261)
DECLARE `s 667(1)(d) the certificate` IS ONE OF
    `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii)`
    `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under paragraph (c)`
    `s 667(1)(d) some other certificate`

-- src:13261 | (d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii) may be in Form 44, and a certificate under paragraph (c) may be in Form 45.
@ref s 667(1)(d) (src:13261-13261)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 667(1)(d) the certificate`
      `the number of the Form` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(1)(d) the certificate may be in the Form` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF certificate EQUALS `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii)` AND `the number of the Form` EQUALS 44 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF certificate EQUALS `s 667(1)(d) a certificate under paragraph (c)` AND `the number of the Form` EQUALS 45 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate under subparagraph (a)(iii) may be in Form 44, and a certificate under paragraph (c) may be in Form 45" (it does not say a certificate may be in no other form)

-- src:13263 | (2) In any proceedings, a copy of the summary conviction or discharge under section 730 in Canada of an offender, signed by the person who made the conviction or order for the discharge or by the clerk of the court in which the conviction or order for the discharge was made, is, on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the copy of the summary conviction, evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant, without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed it.
@ref s 667(2) (src:13263-13263)
GIVEN `the document is a copy of the summary conviction or discharge under section 730 in Canada of an offender, signed by the person who made the conviction or order for the discharge or by the clerk of the court in which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the copy of the summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(2) the copy is evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the document is a copy of the summary conviction or discharge under section 730 in Canada of an offender, signed by the person who made the conviction or order for the discharge or by the clerk of the court in which it was made` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of the summary conviction or discharge under section 730 in Canada of an offender, signed by the person who made the conviction or order for the discharge or by the clerk of the court in which the conviction or order for the discharge was made"
        IF `it is proved that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the copy of the summary conviction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof that the accused or defendant is the offender referred to in the copy of the summary conviction, evidence of the conviction or discharge under section 730 of the accused or defendant" [M-a]

-- src:13265 | (2.1) In any summary conviction proceedings, where the name of a defendant is similar to the name of an offender referred to in a certificate made under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (ii) in respect of a summary conviction or referred to in a copy of a summary conviction mentioned in subsection (2), that similarity of name is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy of the summary conviction.
@ref s 667(2.1) (src:13265-13265)
GIVEN `the proceedings are summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name of a defendant is similar to the name of an offender referred to in a certificate made under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (ii) in respect of a summary conviction or in a copy of a summary conviction mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(2.1) the similarity of name is evidence that the defendant is the offender referred to in the certificate or the copy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are summary conviction proceedings` AND `the name of a defendant is similar to the name of an offender referred to in a certificate made under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (ii) in respect of a summary conviction or in a copy of a summary conviction mentioned in subsection (2)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any summary conviction proceedings, where the name of a defendant is similar to the name of an offender referred to in a certificate made under subparagraph (1)(a)(i) or (ii)"
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, evidence that the defendant is the offender" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13267 | (3) An accused against whom a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref s 667(3) (src:13267-13267)
GIVEN `a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(3) the accused may require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced against the accused` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused against whom a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) is produced"
        IF `the court has given leave` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the person who signed the certificate" [F:may-if]

-- src:13269 | (4) No certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c) shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of his intention together with a copy of the certificate.
@ref s 667(4) (src:13269-13269)
GIVEN `the certificate is a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party intending to produce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the party’s intention together with a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(4) the subsection bars receiving the certificate in evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the certificate is a certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No certificate issued under subparagraph (1)(a)(iii) or paragraph (1)(c)"
        IF `the party intending to produce it has given the accused reasonable notice of the party’s intention together with a copy of the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has given to the accused reasonable notice of his intention together with a copy of the certificate" (the "unless" is met) [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13271 | (5) In this section, fingerprint examiner means a person designated as such for the purposes of this section by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness.
@ref s 667(5) (src:13271-13271)
GIVEN `the person is designated as a fingerprint examiner for the purposes of section 667 by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 667(5) the person is a fingerprint examiner` MEANS
    IF `the person is designated as a fingerprint examiner for the purposes of section 667 by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "fingerprint examiner means a person designated as such for the purposes of this section by the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness" [M-a]

-- src:13272 | 668 and 669 [Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 4]
@ref s 668 and 669 (repealed) (src:13272-13272)
`s 668 and s 669 what the text shows` MEANS "668 and 669 [Repealed, 1995, c. 22, s. 4]"

§ `Sections 669.1 to 669.3 -- Jurisdiction`

-- src:13276 | 669.1 (1) Where any judge, court or provincial court judge by whom or which the plea of the accused or defendant to an offence was taken has not commenced to hear evidence, any judge, court or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication.
@ref s 669.1(1) (src:13276-13276)
GIVEN `a judge, court or provincial court judge by whom or which the plea of the accused or defendant to an offence was taken has not commenced to hear evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.1(1) the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge, court or provincial court judge has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any judge, court or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant has jurisdiction for the purpose of the hearing and adjudication"
        IF `a judge, court or provincial court judge by whom or which the plea of the accused or defendant to an offence was taken has not commenced to hear evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any judge, court or provincial court judge by whom or which the plea of the accused or defendant to an offence was taken has not commenced to hear evidence" [M-a]

-- src:13278 | (2) Any court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try an accused or a defendant, or any clerk or other proper officer of the court, or in the case of an offence punishable on summary conviction, any justice, may, at any time before or after the plea of the accused or defendant is taken, adjourn the proceedings.
@ref s 669.1(2) (src:13278-13278)
DECLARE `s 669.1(2) who adjourns` IS ONE OF
    `s 669.1(2) a court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant`
    `s 669.1(2) a clerk or other proper officer of the court`
    `s 669.1(2) a justice`
    `s 669.1(2) someone else`

-- src:13278 | (2) Any court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try an accused or a defendant, or any clerk or other proper officer of the court, or in the case of an offence punishable on summary conviction, any justice, may, at any time before or after the plea of the accused or defendant is taken, adjourn the proceedings.
@ref s 669.1(2) (src:13278-13278)
GIVEN who IS A `s 669.1(2) who adjourns`
      `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.1(2) the person may adjourn the proceedings at any time before or after the plea is taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `s 669.1(2) a court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF who EQUALS `s 669.1(2) a clerk or other proper officer of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF who EQUALS `s 669.1(2) a justice` AND `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF who EQUALS `s 669.1(2) a justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or in the case of an offence punishable on summary conviction, any justice, may, at any time before or after the plea of the accused or defendant is taken, adjourn the proceedings" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Any court, judge or provincial court judge having jurisdiction to try an accused or a defendant, or any clerk or other proper officer of the court, or in the case of an offence punishable on summary conviction, any justice, may"

DECLARE `s 669.2(1) the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `s 669.2(1)(a) a judge or provincial court judge`
    `s 669.2(1)(b) a justice or other person who is, or is a member of, a summary conviction court`
    `s 669.2(1)(c) a court composed of a judge and jury`
    `s 669.2(1) some other tribunal`

-- src:13280 | 669.2 (1) Subject to this section, where an accused or a defendant is being tried by
-- src:13281 | (a) a judge or provincial court judge,
-- src:13282 | (b) a justice or other person who is, or is a member of, a summary conviction court, or
-- src:13283 | (c) a court composed of a judge and jury,
-- src:13284 | as the case may be, and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue, the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person, as the case may be, who has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant.
@ref s 669.2(1) (src:13280-13284)
GIVEN tribunal IS A `s 669.2(1) the tribunal`
      `the accused or defendant is being tried by the tribunal and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(1) the proceedings may be continued before another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF tribunal EQUALS `s 669.2(1) some other tribunal` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "where an accused or a defendant is being tried by (a) a judge or provincial court judge, (b) a justice or other person who is, or is a member of, a summary conviction court, or (c) a court composed of a judge and jury"
        IF NOT `the accused or defendant is being tried by the tribunal and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an accused or a defendant is being tried by ... and the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person dies or is for any reason unable to continue, the proceedings may be continued" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the other judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "another judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person, as the case may be, who has jurisdiction to try the accused or defendant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13286 | (2) Where a verdict was rendered by a jury or an adjudication was made by a judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the trial was commenced, the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the proceedings are continued shall, without further election by an accused, impose the punishment or make the order that is authorized by law in the circumstances.
@ref s 669.2(2) (src:13286-13286)
GIVEN `a verdict was rendered by a jury or an adjudication was made by the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the trial was commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(2) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must impose the punishment or make the order authorized by law without further election by the accused` MEANS
    IF `a verdict was rendered by a jury or an adjudication was made by the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the trial was commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a verdict was rendered by a jury or an adjudication was made by a judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the trial was commenced, the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the proceedings are continued shall, without further election by an accused, impose the punishment or make the order" [F:duty] [M-a]

-- src:13288 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) and (5), if the trial was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the proceedings are continued shall, without further election by an accused, commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken.
@ref s 669.2(3) (src:13288-13288)
GIVEN `the trial was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial is before a court composed of a judge and a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(3) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued must commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the trial was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trial was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the judge, provincial court judge, justice or other person before whom the proceedings are continued shall, without further election by an accused, commence the trial again" [F:duty] [M-a]
        IF `the trial is before a court composed of a judge and a jury` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsections (4) and (5)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13290 | (4) If a trial that is before a court composed of a judge and a jury was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may, without further election by an accused, continue the trial or commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken.
@ref s 669.2(4) (src:13290-13290)
DECLARE `s 669.2(4) the course` IS ONE OF
    `s 669.2(4) continue the trial`
    `s 669.2(4) commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken`
    `s 669.2(4) some other course`

-- src:13290 | (4) If a trial that is before a court composed of a judge and a jury was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may, without further election by an accused, continue the trial or commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken.
@ref s 669.2(4) (src:13290-13290)
GIVEN `the trial is before a court composed of a judge and a jury, was commenced, and no adjudication was made or verdict rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 669.2(4) the course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(4) the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may take the course without further election by the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the trial is before a court composed of a judge and a jury, was commenced, and no adjudication was made or verdict rendered` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a trial that is before a court composed of a judge and a jury was commenced but no adjudication was made or verdict rendered, the judge before whom the proceedings are continued may" [F:may-if]
        IF course EQUALS `s 669.2(4) some other course` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may, without further election by an accused, continue the trial or commence the trial again as if no evidence on the merits had been taken"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13292 | (5) Where a trial is continued under subsection (4), any evidence that was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c) is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued but, if the prosecutor and the accused consent, any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued.
@ref s 669.2(5) (src:13292-13292)
GIVEN `the trial is continued under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(5) the evidence is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued` MEANS
    IF `the trial is continued under subsection (4)` AND `the evidence was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a trial is continued under subsection (4), any evidence that was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c) is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued" [M-a]

-- src:13292 | (5) Where a trial is continued under subsection (4), any evidence that was adduced before a judge referred to in paragraph (1)(c) is deemed to have been adduced before the judge before whom the trial is continued but, if the prosecutor and the accused consent, any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued.
@ref s 669.2(5) (src:13292-13292)
GIVEN `the trial is continued under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor and the accused consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.2(5) any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the trial is continued under subsection (4)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a trial is continued under subsection (4), ... any part of that evidence may be adduced again before the judge before whom the trial is continued" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF `the prosecutor and the accused consent` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the prosecutor and the accused consent, any part of that evidence may be adduced again" [F:may-if]

-- src:13294 | 669.3 Where a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court, he or she continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial until its completion.
@ref s 669.3 (src:13294-13294)
GIVEN `a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 669.3 the judge or provincial court judge continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court composed of a judge and a jury, a judge or a provincial court judge is conducting a trial and the judge or provincial court judge is appointed to another court, he or she continues to have jurisdiction" [M-a]
        IF `the trial has been completed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "continues to have jurisdiction in respect of the trial until its completion" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
